        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Do you mean **powdered juice** (juice in dry powder form that you mix with water)? Here are a few easy ways—**homemade and safe**.\n\n---\n\n## Method 1: Simple Homemade Fruit Juice Powder (Best & Natural)\n\n### You’ll need\n- Fresh fruit (orange, mango, strawberry, apple, etc.)\n- Blender\n- Oven **or** food dehydrator\n- Grinder / blender\n- Fine sieve\n- Airtight container\n\n### Steps\n1. **Wash & cut fruit**  \n   Remove seeds and peels if needed.\n\n2. **Blend into juice or puree**  \n   Add a little water only if required.\n\n3. **Strain (optional)**  \n   For clearer juice powder, strain out pulp.\n\n4. **Dry the juice**\n   - **Oven method:**  \n     - Line a tray with parchment paper  \n     - Spread juice thinly  \n     - Dry at **60–70°C (140–160°F)** for several hours  \n   - **Dehydrator:**  \n     - Dry until completely brittle\n\n5. **Grind into powder**  \n   Break dried sheets and grind finely.\n\n6. **Sieve & store**  \n   Store in an airtight jar away from moisture.\n\n7. **Use**  \n   Mix **1–2 tsp powder + water** 🍹\n\n---\n\n## Method 2: Quick Powder Using Juice + Carrier (Easier)\n\nThis prevents clumping.\n\n### Extra ingredient\n- **Maltodextrin OR cornstarch (very small amount)**\n\n### Steps\n1. Mix **fresh juice + 1–2 tsp maltodextrin**\n2. Dry as above\n3. Grind → free-flowing powder\n\n---\n\n## Method 3: Instant Flavor Powder (Not Natural Juice)\n\n- Sugar\n- Citric acid\n- Fruit flavor powder\n- Food coloring (optional)\n\n👉 This is how **store-bought powdered juice** is made, but it’s not real juice.\n\n---\n\n## Tips\n- Must be **completely dry** or it will spoil\n- Add **vitamin C powder** for longer shelf life\n- Keep away from humidity\n\nIf you want, tell me:\n- 🍊 Which fruit?\n- 🏠 Home or small business?\n- 💪 Health-focused or taste-focused?\n\nI’ll tailor it exactly for you."
          ]
        },
